-- title:
--   Realising T_q in the local Hecke algebra with value a
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over the residue field $k$ of $\mathcal O$, factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, whose base change to $\overline{k}$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, let $q\in S$ be a prime with $q\ne p$, and let $N,L\ge 1$ satisfy $q\nmid N$, $L\mid N$ and: every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$. Assume weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by those with integral $q$-expansion coefficients, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^S(N)$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_{q'}$, $q'\mid N$, $q'\notin S$) to $k$ such that at every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $\pi_T$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the localisation $\mathbb T^S(N)_\theta$ to $\mathcal O$, with structural map $\pi$, and let $a\in\mathcal O$ be such that there exists a rank-$2$ free $\mathcal O$-module with adically continuous Galois action whose characteristic polynomial at Frobenius at each $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid N$, is $X^2-\pi_T(\pi(T_\ell))X+\ell$, which is unramified at $q$ (inertia at every place over $q$ acts trivially) and has trace $a$ at every Frobenius element at $q$. On the cohomological carrier $H^1(L):=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(L)^{\mathrm{ab}},\mathcal O)$ let the family of operators indexed by the symbols $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$), $U_{q'}$ ($q'\mid L$) and $\langle d\rangle$ be assumed pairwise commuting; let $\bar\theta$ assign a residue-field value to each such symbol, let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ in the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by these operators, with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ enumerating all maximal ideals and $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j$ exactly for $i\ne j$, fix an index $i_0$, and let $\pi_k$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the corner ring at $i_0$ to $k$ sending the image of each generator to its $\bar\theta$-value. Assume $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and $\ell\nmid N$, that every element of the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H^1(L)$ is parabolic (vanishes on elements of trace square $4$), and let $M$ be an $\mathcal O$-module and $\mathbb T^S(N)_\theta$-module, compatibly, together with an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ of $M$ onto $e_{i_0}H^1(L)$ carrying the action of $\pi(T_\ell)$ to the Hecke operator $T_\ell$ on $H^1(L)$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$. Then there is an element $t$ of $\mathbb T^S(N)_\theta$ whose action on $M$ corresponds under $e$ to the Hecke operator $T_q$ on $H^1(L)$, and which satisfies $\pi_T(t)=a$.
--
--   This supplies the input for the level-raising step at a prime $q\nmid N$: the operator $T_q$ at an auxiliary prime $q\in S$ is exhibited inside the localised anemic Hecke algebra acting on a corner of the cohomology of $\Gamma_0(L)$, and its value under a given point $\pi_T$ is identified with the Frobenius trace at $q$ of the associated $\mathcal O$-adic representation. It is used in the construction of corner realisations and of the rungs of the level-raising tower.
